    {
      "id": "concept-google-plus-facebook-comparison",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "unirte · como · qué demonios · en realidad",
      "questionEn": "Why does the final change of mind make the social-network exchange a joke?",
      "answerEn": "The listener first resists a new service because it is described as Facebook, then suddenly realizes that a Facebook-like service was what he wanted.",
      "noteEn": "Google+ launched as a social network in 2011 and was commonly compared with Facebook. The blank middle panel gives the listener time to reconsider. The official title text adds a two-sided joke: parents being hard to persuade to switch is both a disadvantage and an advantage of a new network.",
      "tags": [
        "concept",
